{
    "background_story": "Marco, the Duke of Tuscany, was a just and fair ruler, beloved by his people. His lordship was marked by wisdom, compassion, and strength. He inherited the title from his father, but it was his own character that earned him the respect and admiration of his subjects. Marco was a patron of the arts, and his court attracted scholars, poets, and musicians from all over Europe. He was a skilled diplomat, navigating the complex web of alliances and rivalries between the city-states of Italy. Marco's greatest achievement was the establishment of a fair and equitable system of justice, which brought peace and prosperity to his lands. His people prospered under his lordship, and his name became synonymous with wisdom, honor, and nobility.",
